{"step_index":240,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T17:26:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-06T19:26:24+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-06T19:26:24+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 135\nTotal Bytes: 6007\nShowing lines 50 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n50: \n51: - **Branching Strategy**: Standard GitFlow model (`main`, `develop`, `feature/*`, `bugfix/*`).\n52: - **Static Code Analysis**: Maven Checkstyle plugin enforcing strict Java coding standards.\n53: - **Code Coverage Gate**: JaCoCo Maven plugin enforcing minimum line coverage thresholds.\n54: - **Continuous Deployment**: Multi-stage, minimal attack surface JRE Docker image with non-root security execution.\n55: \n56: ---\n57: \n58: ## 🚀 Prerequisites & Quick Start\n59: \n60: ### Option 1: Run Locally with Maven & Java 17+\n61: ```bash\n62: # Clone the repository\n63: git clone <your-repository-url>\n64: cd qualification-verification-system\n65: \n66: # Run tests and verify build\n67: mvn clean test\n68: \n69: # Launch the Spring Boot application (Dev Profile / In-Memory H2 DB)\n70: mvn spring-boot:run\n71: ```\n72: The application will be accessible at: **`http://localhost:8080`**\n73: \n74: ### Option 2: Run with Docker Compose (PostgreSQL Production Setup)\n75: ```bash\n76: docker compose up --build\n77: ```\n78: This boots both the **Spring Boot application** and a dedicated **PostgreSQL 15** database container.\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 🧪 Automated Testing & Quality Gates\n83: \n84: Run the comprehensive unit and integration test suite:\n85: ```bash\n86: # Execute unit and integration tests\n87: mvn clean test\n88: \n89: # Generate JaCoCo code coverage