{"step_index":242,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T17:26:24Z","content":"Here are the complete, step-by-step instructions to run the **Qualification Verification System (QVS)** on any new machine (Windows, macOS, or Linux).\n\nYou can choose whichever method best fits the new environment:\n- **Option 1 (Easiest / No Tools needed except Docker):** One-Click with Docker Compose.\n- **Option 2 (Local Development):** Using Java 17 and the included scripts/Maven wrapper.\n- **Option 3 (Lightweight Production):** Running the pre-packaged Standalone `.jar`.\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ Option 1: One-Click Docker Run (Recommended)\n*Use this if the new machine has **Docker Desktop** installed. No Java or Maven installation is required.*\n\n1. **Copy or Clone the Project** to the new machine:\n   ```bash\n   git clone <your-repository-url>\n   cd qualification-verification-system\n   ```\n2. **Launch Application & PostgreSQL with Docker Compose:**\n   ```bash\n   docker compose up --build\n   ```\n3. **Open Your Browser:**\n   Navigate to: **`http://localhost:8080`**\n\n*Both the Spring Boot backend and the PostgreSQL database container will start automatically with health checks enabled.*\n\n---\n\n## ☕ Option 2: Running Locally with Java 17 (Host Machine)\n\n### Step 1: Install Java 17\n1. Ensure **Java 17 (JDK)** is installed. \n   - [Download Eclipse Temurin 17 (Adoptium)](https://adoptium.net/temurin/releases/?version=17) or Oracle JDK 17.\n2. Verify Java is recognized:\n   ```bash\n   java -version\n   ```\n   *(You should see `openjdk version \"17.x.x\"`).*\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Run the App\n\n#### On Windows:\nYou can either:\n- **Double-click** the file: **[`run-app.bat`](file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/run-app.bat)**  \n  *(OR open PowerShell / Command Prompt inside the folder and run)*:\n  ```cmd\n  .\\run-app.bat\n  ```\n- **OR use the cross-platform Maven wrapper** *(No Maven installation needed)*:\n  ```cmd\n  mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run\n  ```\n\n#### On macOS / Linux:\nOpen Terminal inside the project root:\n```bash\nchmod +x mvnw\n./mvnw spring-boot:run\n```\n*(If Maven is already installed on the machine, you can also simply run `mvn spring-boot:run`).*\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Access the Web Portal\nOnce the terminal displays `Started QualificationVerificationApplication in X seconds`:\n- **Web Portal:** `http://localhost:8080`\n- **Swagger OpenAPI Documentation:** `http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html`\n- **Actuator Health & Metrics:** `http://localhost:8080/actuator/health`\n\n---\n\n## 📦 Option 3: Running as a Standalone Executable JAR\n*If you just want to run the single binary file without building:*\n\n1. **Package the `.jar`** (only once):\n   ```bash\n   mvnw.cmd clean package -DskipTests      # Windows\n   ./mvnw clean package -DskipTests        # Mac/Linux\n   ```\n2. **Execute the JAR on the new machine:**\n   ```bash\n   java -jar target/qualification-verification-system-2.0.0.jar\n   ```\n3. **Open:** `http://localhost:8080`\n\n---\n\n## 🧪 How to Run Automated Tests on a New Machine\n\nTo verify that all 35 automated tests and JaCoCo coverage quality gates pass on the new machine:\n\n- **Windows:** Double-click [`run-tests.bat`](file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/run-tests.bat) or run:\n  ```cmd\n  mvnw.cmd clean test jacoco:report\n  ```\n- **macOS / Linux:**\n  ```bash\n  ./mvnw clean test jacoco:report\n  ```\n*View the generated HTML coverage report at: `target/site/jacoco/index.html`.*\n\n---\n\n## 🔑 Pre-Seeded Demo Credentials for Testing\n\n| Role | Username | Password | Access / Capabilities |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **System Administrator** | `admin` | `Admin@123` | Full access, revoke records, view audit trails |\n| **Institution Officer** | `institution` | `Inst@123` | Issue and register new degrees/diplomas |\n| **Corporate Verifier** | `verifier` | `Verify@123` | High-volume batch verification |\n| **Public / Guest** | *(No login)* | *(None)* | Instant public certificate verification |\n\n### Sample Certificates to Test Immediately on the Home Page:\n- `QVS-2024-BSC-8891` (Sarah Jenkins) $\\rightarrow$ Displays **GENUINE & VALID** (Green badge)\n- `QVS-2023-MSC-4412` (Elena Rostova) $\\rightarrow$ Displays **GENUINE & VALID** (Green badge)\n- `QVS-2022-DIP-1109` (Marcus Vance) $\\rightarrow$ Displays **REVOKED CREDENTIAL** (Red badge with disciplinary audit note)"}
